<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attĭca</span></b> , ae, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attĭcē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀττική</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The most distinguished province of Greece</i>, <i>situated in Hellas proper</i>, <i>with
				Athens as capital.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attĭca</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun. 1, 2,
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attĭcē</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 1, § 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 7, 11, §
			23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attĭca</span></b> , <i>the name of the daughter of T. Pompomus
			Atticus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 12, 1</span></i>; cf. Atticula.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
